{"name":"Shallow Sea","hex":"#9ab8c2","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shallow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having little depth; significantly less deep than wide.","Extending not far downward."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shallow portion of an otherwise deep body of water.","A fish, the rudd."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shallow"},{"term":"sea","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Semai."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large body of salt water.","The ocean; the continuous body of salt water covering a majority of the Earth's surface."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sea"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shallow water marine environment","blocks":[{"text":"Shallow water marine environment refers to the neritic marine environment between the shore and the shelf break. This environment is characterized by oceanic, geological and biological conditions, as described below, and water in this environment is shallow and clear, allowing the formation of different sedimentary structures, carbonate rocks, coral reefs, and allowing certain organisms to survive and become fossils."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Shallow_water.jpg/330px-Shallow_water.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shallow_water_marine_environment"},{"title":"Sea","blocks":[{"text":"A sea is a very large body of salty water. The term has two distinct meanings. The first is the interconnected body of seawater that spans most of Earth, known as the sea or the ocean. The second is a named body of water: usually either a marginal sea, or a large, nearly landlocked body of water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/330px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api